Platform: the same Gaudi 3 server before the out-of-tree habanalabs driver is
installed: eight 0x1da3:0x1060 functions, no driver, no accel nodes. k3d-gpu must
warn and skip Gaudi; the host's AMX is still detected.

Sources (kernel paths are Linux v6.18 (torvalds/linux tag v6.18)):
- 0x1da3 0x1060 "Gaudi3 AI Training Accelerator": pci.ids 2026.10.15
  (pciutils/pciids). Mainline lists only up to Gaudi2 (0x1020,
  drivers/accel/habanalabs/common/habanalabs_drv.c), so Gaudi 3 means Intel's
  out-of-tree habanalabs driver; module name and accel layout match mainline.
- /dev/accel/accel<n> and /sys/class/accel/accel<n>: Documentation/accel/introduction.rst.
- accel_controlD<n> beside accel<n>, same index: drivers/accel/habanalabs/common/device.c
  (snprintf "accel_controlD%d", cdev_idx = drm.accel->index).
- DSA 0x8086:0x0b25 / IAA 0x8086:0x0cfe, class 0x088000, driver idxd, devices
  dsa0/iax1 (one id space): include/linux/pci_ids.h, drivers/dma/idxd/init.c
  ("%s%d" with name_prefix dsa/iax); class from intel-device-plugins v0.37.1
  deployments/nfd/overlays/node-feature-rules (class 0880).
- ASPEED 0x1a03:0x2000 "ASPEED Graphics Family", driver ast, card0 only: pci.ids.
- amx_bf16 amx_tile amx_int8: arch/x86/include/asm/cpufeatures.h; NFD v0.19.0
  docs/usage/features.md names the labels AMXBF16, AMXTILE, AMXINT8.

Layout: sysfs paths and relative symlinks follow the driver core's naming
(class devices under <pci dev>/<class>/<name>; /sys/class/<class>/<name> and
/sys/bus/pci/devices/<bdf> as relative links; <dev>/driver -> bus/pci/drivers/<drv>),
in exactly the form tests/fixtures/capture.sh writes (the matrix test re-captures
each tree and requires an identical result).

Not from hardware: BDFs, the Gaudi PCI class (0x120000; k3d-gpu does not read
it), the kernel release string, and the cpuinfo flags line (a representative
subset in cpufeatures.h order).
